{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>[Why do you disturb the people]</b> — [they are] idle from Pharaoh's labors. <b>Go to your burdens.</b> The reason: why did the tribe of Levi merit to be free from the bondage of Egypt? When Egypt first enslaved Israel, Pharaoh enslaved himself together with them, so that they would exert themselves in the labor — as we expound בפרך, with a soft mouth. At that time, the tribe of Levi remembered what Jacob commanded at the time of his passing — that Levi should not carry him — because he was destined to carry the holy ark. And he did not wish to enslave himself, and Pharaoh did not force them. From that day onward, it was established that whoever had enslaved himself would be enslaved. And furthermore, it is found in the Aggadah: Abraham handed down the entire tradition of Torah to Isaac, and Isaac to Jacob, and Jacob to Levi. And Levi and his descendants established academies in Egypt. And because they knew no craft and had not engaged in it, but their entire occupation was in Torah, they were not enslaved in Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:17.365442725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}